  "insertion": "\n\n  - id: design-implementation-existing-codebase\n    prompt: \"Implement this approved UI concept inside the existing app. Make it interactive and keep going until it is verified.\"\n    expected_skills: [design-implementation]\n    optional_skills: [change-analysis, implementation-execution, frontend-verification]\n    required_behaviors:\n      - recover the existing codebase ownership and state contracts before editing\n      - map material design regions and behaviors to existing or justified new code\n      - prefer a minimal coherent slice inside the real app over a detached prototype\n      - run and observe the strongest available build test render and interaction evidence\n      - continue through critique revision and reverification rather than stopping at the first render\n\n  - id: design-implementation-no-fake-interactivity\n    prompt: \"The concept includes a new workspace control, but the current product has no such capability. Implement the rest of the concept in the existing codebase.\"\n    expected_skills: [design-implementation]\n    optional_skills: [product-ui-design, design-dna-synthesis]\n    required_behaviors:\n      - classify the new control as proposed rather than existing capability\n      - do not make the control appear operational without an honest product behavior\n      - wire observed capabilities to real product state\n      - keep the proposed affordance explicitly prototypal disabled or implement its product contract with proportionate scope\n\n  - id: design-implementation-render-verification\n    prompt: \"The UI compiles and the first render looks close to the concept. Continue.\"\n    expected_skills: [design-implementation]\n    optional_skills: [frontend-verification, artifact-quality]\n    required_behaviors:\n      - treat compilation and first render as untermediate evidence rather than completion\n      - exercise material interactions and state transitions when the runtime provides direct observation\n      - check responsive keyboard focus console and runtime evidence for the affected surface\n      - classify material faps and revise the smallest surface that resolves them\n      - do not reuse prior certification after a mutation invalidates it\"
